{
  "about": "Rounding a load to what a gym can make, and the plates per side (K-414, ADR-032). The backend (LoadStepsTests) and the app (K-417) read these same cases, so the two implementations agree. Loads in kg, 2 decimals (ADR-029). round: the engine's target after the last load -> the nearest load the gym can make that is heavier than the last; a tie goes to the lighter; NO_HEAVIER when the gym has nothing heavier (only a finite list can end: dumbbells, or a bodyweight move's dumbbells without plates); UNKNOWN when the gym says nothing about this equipment. A gym whose weights were entered in lb (each on the quarter-pound grid, at least one not a multiple of 0.05 kg) is counted in hundredths of a lb, and a load goes back to kg as the app converts a typed lb load (round(lb x 0.45359237, 2)): 140 lb is 63.5, whatever plates make it. platesPerSide: fewest plates, heavier first on a tie; null when the total cannot be made.",
